{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "prefix-extension-policy-depth-diagnostic",
    "parent": "throughput-to-depth-reinvestment",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Instrument why prefix depth saturates at ~3.3 independent of a 16x iteration budget",
    "description": "Add per-run diagnostic counters to the explorer/prefix scheduler (the code path that emits meanPrefixDepth/depthAtLeast in utilStats) recording, per terminal run: the depth reached, whether a deeper extension was PROPOSED but rejected, and the rejection reason bucket (no distinguishable pending event at the frontier, dedup/hash hit on an already-explored prefix, depth cap hit, step/iteration budget hit). Surface as a new utilStats block (e.g. utilStats.prefixExtension) alongside utilStats.termination, gated by an existing verbose/stats flag in scheduler_configs/loop/general_vr.json so it is off by default. No behavior change. The 1500->24000 iteration sweep shows depthAtLeast[7] is flat at ~0.0014 across a 16x budget range, so the binding constraint is one of the non-budget buckets; we currently cannot tell which.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "prefix depth cap",
      "explorer step budget",
      "utilStats termination counters"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 6,
    "expectedCost": 1.5,
    "rationale": "Every depth-directed hypothesis so far has been a blind knob turn; this one measurement partitions the depth ceiling into budget-bound vs frontier-bound vs dedup-bound and tells the pool which family of interventions can possibly work. Cheap, no new mechanism, and it converts the flat-tail observation above into an actionable cause.",
    "generalityArgument": "Pure counter instrumentation on the protocol-agnostic prefix scheduler; no spec knowledge, no VR-specific fields, and it is read-only with respect to scheduling decisions so it cannot bias any spec's exploration.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-30T00:20:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "Directly motivated by the flat depthAtLeast[7] across grid-short/grid/grid-deep in eval 1001. [rejudged iteration 5340: Up-scored: throughput-to-depth-reinvestment proved depth is capped by the extension policy, not by step/iteration budget (76% utilization at 16x budget, flat per-arm d>=7), so the rejection-reason bucket is now the only live route to the per-run factor of the primary; falsified i"
  },
